# A WATCHPOST ON OPEN DECK, AND ROOM TO SHOOT AT IT FROM.
#
# The fixture for M23 phase 5. Not the generated case -- a section places a patch
# wherever its safe corridor allows, and a test that has to find the tower first
# is a test measuring the placement rule rather than the thing on top of it.
#
# NOTHING ELSE IS IN HERE. No holes, no other height, no hazards: the question is
# whether a round from the deck reaches a turret three units up, and every other
# feature on the map is a way for that question to be answered by accident. Same
# rule as the ramp measurements -- measure on a fixture with nothing else moving
# in it.
#
# The post is column 7, rows 5-6, three units up, with a ladder at row 5 and the
# turret on top at row 6. The deck runs flat for four rows in front of it so a
# shot is taken at a real engagement distance rather than from underneath.

name = test_watchpost
base_height = 0
width = 15
length = 12
tags = fixture, watchpost

